{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791339979557,"sessionID":"ses_eebd28287ffe4uKSFxrZYOYb26","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"31DP868Z3tQqBhN4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/user/auto-psych/data/rsa/loop_smoke2/round_1/candidate_2/existing_hypotheses.md"},"output":"<path>/home/user/auto-psych/data/rsa/loop_smoke2/round_1/candidate_2/existing_hypotheses.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Models in the set\n2: \n3: ## literal_listener (1478.4 ± 49.4 nats behind the best)\n4: \n5: Listeners pick uniformly among the objects the word is literally true of.\n6: \n7: Source: `data/rsa/loop_smoke2/models/literal_listener.py`\n8: \n9: ## rsa_l1 (47.8 ± 3.9 nats behind the best)\n10: \n11: Listeners invert a softmax-rational speaker who simulates a literal listener (depth 1), with a uniform prior over objects.\n12: \n13: Source: `data/rsa/loop_smoke2/models/rsa_l1.py`\n14: \n15: ## rsa_l2 (best)\n16: \n17: Listeners reason one level deeper (depth 2), inverting a speaker who simulates the depth-1 pragmatic listener.\n18: \n19: Source: `data/rsa/loop_smoke2/models/rsa_l2.py`\n20: \n21: ## rsa_l1_salience (13.0 ± 8.4 nats behind the best)\n22: \n23: Depth-1 RSA whose listener has a salience prior over objects (feature count, familiarization base rate) that the simulated literal listener lacks.\n24: \n25: Source: `data/rsa/loop_smoke2/models/rsa_l1_salience.py`\n26: \n27: ## rsa_l1_shared_prior (9.1 ± 8.5 nats behind the best)\n28: \n29: Depth-1 RSA with the salience prior as common knowledge, used by the simulated literal listener as well as the pragmatic listener.\n30: \n31: Source: `data/rsa/loop_smoke2/models/rsa_l1_shared_prior.py`\n\n(End of file - total 31 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Models in the set\n\n## literal_listener (1478.4 ± 49.4 nats behind the best)\n\nListeners pick uniformly among the objects the word is literally true of.\n\nSource: `data/rsa/loop_smoke2/models/literal_listener.py`\n\n## rsa_l1 (47.8 ± 3.9 nats behind the best)\n\nListeners invert a softmax-rational speaker who simulates a literal listener (depth 1), with a uniform prior over objects.\n\nSource: `data/rsa/loop_smoke2/models/rsa_l1.py`\n\n## rsa_l2 (best)\n\nListeners reason one level deeper (depth 2), inverting a speaker who simulates the depth-1 pragmatic listener.\n\nSource: `data/rsa/loop_smoke2/models/rsa_l2.py`\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/user/auto-psych/data/rsa/loop_smoke2/round_1/candidate_2/existing_hypotheses.md","text":"# Models in the set\n\n## literal_listener (1478.4 ± 49.4 nats behind the best)\n\nListeners pick uniformly among the objects the word is literally true of.\n\nSource: `data/rsa/loop_smoke2/models/literal_listener.py`\n\n## rsa_l1 (47.8 ± 3.9 nats behind the best)\n\nListeners invert a softmax-rational speaker who simulates a literal listener (depth 1), with a uniform prior over objects.\n\nSource: `data/rsa/loop_smoke2/models/rsa_l1.py`\n\n## rsa_l2 (best)\n\nListeners reason one level deeper (depth 2), inverting a speaker who simulates the depth-1 pragmatic listener.\n\nSource: `data/rsa/loop_smoke2/models/rsa_l2.py`\n\n## rsa_l1_salience (13.0 ± 8.4 nats behind the best)\n\nDepth-1 RSA whose listener has a salience prior over objects (feature count, familiarization base rate) that the simulated literal listener lacks.\n\nSource: `data/rsa/loop_smoke2/models/rsa_l1_salience.py`\n\n## rsa_l1_shared_prior (9.1 ± 8.5 nats behind the best)\n\nDepth-1 RSA with the salience prior as common knowledge, used by the simulated literal listener as well as the pragmatic listener.\n\nSource: `data/rsa/loop_smoke2/models/rsa_l1_shared_prior.py`","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":31,"totalLines":31,"truncated":false}},"title":"data/rsa/loop_smoke2/round_1/candidate_2/existing_hypotheses.md","time":{"start":1791339979503,"end":1791339979524}},"metadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}},"id":"prt_1142ee2e4001Lg2C1WVXl4BpoY","sessionID":"ses_eeb